-- Passage rg7-authors-purpose-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4864e71e-7b0d-5518-857c-76151de57e80', 'rg7-authors-purpose-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-authors-purpose'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Keep the Library Open on Saturdays$q$, $q$The Maple Street branch library is open six days a week, but next month that will change. To save money, the library board plans to close the branch every Saturday. I understand that the budget is tight. Still, I think closing on Saturdays is the wrong choice, and I hope readers will tell the board so.

Saturday is the only day many families can visit. Parents who work long hours during the week cannot bring their children after school. Students who play sports or care for younger siblings often have no free time until the weekend. Last year, the branch counted more visitors on Saturdays than on any other day of the week.

Board members say the branch could stay open later on Tuesday evenings instead. They argue that this change would keep the total number of open hours the same. On paper, that sounds fair. However, a Tuesday evening does not help a family whose parents work until nine o'clock. It also does not help the Saturday reading club, which meets at ten in the morning and has more than thirty young members.

There are other ways to save money. The branch could share one delivery van with the Elm Road branch, or it could print fewer paper flyers and post more news online. These steps would not take away a whole day from the people who need the library most.

A library is only useful when people can walk through its doors. Please attend the board meeting on the fourteenth and ask the board to keep Saturdays.$q$, 'draft')
