  ('8b5cee86-7624-5467-a8a2-fa50233b92ee', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which common belief does the author challenge?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Songbirds need insects to eat in the early spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-supporting-point"},{"text":"A thick layer of wet leaves can harm a grassy lawn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-concession"},{"text":"A neat yard with every leaf removed is a healthy yard.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Leaves return nutrients to the soil as they break down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-supporting-point"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A neat yard with every leaf removed is a healthy yard.$q$, $q$The author opens by describing homeowners who "believe a neat yard is a healthy yard" and then argues leaves are "not trash." The author agrees that wet leaves can harm a lawn, so that belief is not challenged.$q$, 'draft', '71a7b235-a699-57a7-b069-49186598661c')
