  ('d0077d9a-00de-5b87-9336-ee7942dc187c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the author's response to Mr. Okafor shape the author's final position?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author agrees with him completely and decides that every leaf should be bagged after all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-position"},{"text":"The author accepts his point and recommends mowing leaves on lawns and moving the rest into beds.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author rejects his point and insists that leaves should be left everywhere in the yard.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The author ignores his point and adds more facts about beetles, spiders, and earthworms.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-counterargument"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author accepts his point and recommends mowing leaves on lawns and moving the rest into beds.$q$, $q$The author says "He is right about that" and explains, "That is why I do not leave leaves everywhere," then describes mowing and raking leaves into beds. The author still keeps the leaves, so the position is adjusted, not abandoned.$q$, 'draft', '71a7b235-a699-57a7-b069-49186598661c')
