  ('be19e5ee-b335-53ed-947c-9e6f00b10072', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Why does the author write, "When we bag the leaves, we bag up part of the food chain"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To argue that homeowners should start feeding songbirds with seeds during the winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To admit that bagging leaves is a useful way to protect the food chain from frost.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-purpose"},{"text":"To tell readers that animals are often trapped and carried away inside bags of leaves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To help readers see that an ordinary chore can remove food and shelter that wildlife needs.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To help readers see that an ordinary chore can remove food and shelter that wildlife needs.$q$, $q$The sentence ends a paragraph about creatures that shelter in leaves and the birds that eat them, so it connects raking to its effect on wildlife. It is a figurative way of describing loss, not a literal claim about trapped animals.$q$, 'draft', '71a7b235-a699-57a7-b069-49186598661c')
