   $q$How does the author use the comparison of a plain gray wall to "an empty page"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the author thinks gray paint is the cheapest choice for the city right now.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"To admit that a mural would probably be covered with new tags within a few months.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-purpose"},{"text":"To suggest the students should write a story on the wall instead of painting a picture.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To suggest a blank wall invites tags, turning the director's worry into a reason for a mural.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To suggest a blank wall invites tags, turning the director's worry into a reason for a mural.$q$, $q$The comparison follows "the evidence points the other way," meaning a blank wall tempts taggers while a community mural seems "worth protecting." The author uses it to argue against the tagging concern, not to admit it.$q$, 'draft', '149f235a-7156-50bf-a282-bd3f18a3be01')
